\"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"MT-Bench expert drop top-1 fraction 2.74%, flip 1.37%.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_human_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_human_top1_flip_frac\",\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"MT-Bench GPT-4 judge drop top-1 fraction 5.96%, flip 2.54%.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_gpt4_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_gpt4_top1_flip_frac\",\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"NBA season-mean top-1 fractions are 0.876% (drop) and 0.457% (flip); per-season drop fractions 0.531% and 1.22%.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.nba_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.nba_top1_flip_frac\",\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Row counts n derived as k divided by the reported fraction: Arena 135,622; MT-Bench expert 3,355; GPT-4 judge 2,400; NBA 2014 1,319 and NBA 2015 1,311 (2x2 system).\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.arena140k_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_human_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_gpt4_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.nba_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.nba_top1_flip_frac\",\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Influence-ordered sets are about 15.7x smaller than random perturbations: mean clipped log2 ratio 3.975, 95% CI [3.934, 4.0], censored at the clip of 4.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.mean_log2_ratio_vs_random\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_log2_ratio_vs_random_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_log2_ratio_vs_random_ci_high\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Sizes coincide with the one-step influence comparator: mean log2 ratio 0.0, CI [0.0, 0.0]; equal top-1 drop fractions.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.mean_log2_ratio_vs_amip\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_log2_ratio_vs_amip_ci_low\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_log2_ratio_vs_amip_ci_high\",\n        \"final.metric.arena140k_top1_drop_frac_amip\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_human_top1_drop_frac_amip\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_gpt4_top1_drop_frac_amip\",\n        \"final.metric.nba_top1_drop_frac_amip\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [\n        \"Broderick2020AnAF\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The pre-declared superiority test over the influence ordering is not supported.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.claim_supported\",\n        \"final.metric.mean_log2_ratio_vs_amip_ci_low\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Direct heuristic family scores are 0 for Arena, GPT-4 judge and NBA, and -0.0053 for MT-Bench experts; under the harness's stated (uninspectable) scoring rule the heuristic was marginally smaller in at least one MT-Bench-expert case.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.arena140k_score\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_gpt4_score\",\n        \"final.metric.nba_score\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_human_score\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The planted synthetic control returns k=8 with control score 0, which under the harness's stated score definition equals its enumerated minimum.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.synthetic_control_score\",\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The row-permutation control returns 62, identical to the Arena drop top-1 size (score 0).\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.metric.permutation_control_score\",\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"All 15 real-case sizes are identical across seeds 101, 102 and 103; replay match 1.0; failed-episode fraction 0.0.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"final.metric.replay_match\",\n        \"final.metric.failed_episode_fraction\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The sealed evaluation completed, qualified, and passed all validity gates.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.qualification.status\",\n        \"final.qualification.outcome\",\n        \"final.qualification.correct\",\n        \"final.metric.final_correct\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Drop-to-flip ratios for top-1 are 1.35, 2.0, 2.34, 1.75 and 2.0; flipping is always cheaper.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"For MT-Bench the GPT-4 leader needs more drops for top-1 (143 vs 92; 5.96% vs 2.74%) but fewer for top-3 (150 vs 229; 6.25% vs 6.83%).\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_gpt4_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.mtbench_human_top1_drop_frac\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [\n        \"Zheng2023JudgingLW\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Fragility ordering of drop top-1 cases reverses between count (NBA 7, 16 before Arena 62) and fraction (Arena 0.0457% first).\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"final.metric.arena140k_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.nba_top1_drop_frac\",\n        \"final.metric.nba_top1_flip_frac\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Recorded episode time per seed over all 17 cases was 15.99 s, 15.55 s and 16.33 s.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The evaluated configuration is the baseline influence ordering; the three refined search configurations were all unscored (0 of 3 scored), the cause is not recorded, and their effect is unknown, not a loss.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"study.selection_kind\",\n        \"study.attempts.total\",\n        \"study.attempts.unscored\",\n        \"study.attempts.scored\",\n        \"study.investigation_outcome\",\n        \"study.search_score_delta\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Exact search and lower-bound certificates for minimal drop sets are computationally demanding beyond a few dimensions even for least squares, so heuristic sets are upper bounds.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"ref.s2.e0a2d58bae2e9586ef61541960c0cb9eab3cd213\",\n        \"ref.s2.b2434a9a214c4b1eea48961c1afb0ced8faefcc5\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [\n        \"Freund2023TowardsPR\",\n        \"Moitra2022ProvablyAO\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Ranking recovery under BTL-type models with a fraction of adversarially corrupted comparisons is the setting the flip perturbation instantiates.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"ref.s2.fcb8fca2cc4de6fe4345a751595b9831eeff2b65\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [\n        \"Patil2020RankAF\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"BT models are used for sports tournaments; we fit a static BT per NBA season.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"ref.s2.692e25e72324616232affbadc403d9d7e4499faa\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [\n        \"Cattelan2013DynamicBM\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}{\n  \"bibtex_key_count\": 30,\n  \"citation_count\": 30,\n  \"claim_count\": 24,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"evidence_validation\": {\n    \"bundle_path\": \"work/results/t06/claude/20261028_222957/paper/scientific-evidence\",\n    \"bundle_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"danglin